{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Bring</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the other two: \"bring the men home\" (Genesis 43:16), \"come to the city.\" Regarding Jonathan ben Joseph it is written \"bring the men home\" — for through him they came to Egypt. And concerning Moses it is said \"bring your hand\" — for through him they departed from there. \"Come to the city\" — a hint that through him they will be gathered and come to the city, which is Jerusalem, as it is written: \"like a city that is joined together\" (Psalms 122:3)." "<b>In your bosom</b> Three times in the Masorah: here one, and two regarding David: \"and I will give your master's wives into your bosom\" (II Samuel 12:8), \"and lie in your bosom\" (II Samuel 12:11). Just as Moses was stricken with tzara'at, so Ruth was stricken with tzara'at, as the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded that she was afflicted [with tzara'at] for six months."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:51.200423433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}